  "summary": "Package contains hardcoded Telegram C2 with host reconnaissance and shell execution",
  "details": "The package ships multiple files that combine child_process, filesystem, and outbound HTTPS in a shape consistent with host reconnaissance and remote-control. health.js and setup.js contain hardcoded requests to https://api.telegram.org (a common C2 channel using bot tokens as a message bus), alongside reads of process.env, process.platform, and process.version and filesystem enumeration via fs.existsSync. bot.js pairs require(\"child_process\") with https POSTs and directory enumeration (fs.readdirSync). core/scheduler.js invokes spawn(\"sh\",...), and core/handlers.js runs whoami/hostname and POSTs results outward. channels/voice/adapter.js runs ping and POSTs. The combined pattern across setup.js (install/setup-time script), health.js, and bot.js — host identifier collection plus environment reads plus outbound HTTPS to api.telegram.org plus shell execution — matches a Telegram-bot-based command-and-control fingerprint rather than a documented feature of a Claude-related tool.",
